Boat Binder operational health alert

Detected at: <%= @detected_at %>

Boat Binder detected one or more application health conditions. This message contains only sanitized aggregates. It excludes job arguments, exception messages, attachment names, storage keys, customer data, and vessel data.

<% @conditions.each do |condition| %>
<% case condition[:category] %>
<% when "failed_background_jobs" %>
Failed background jobs: <%= condition[:total_count] %>
<% condition[:groups].each do |group| %>
- <%= group[:job_class] %>: <%= group[:count] %> failure(s); first <%= group[:first_failed_at] %>; most recent <%= group[:most_recent_failed_at] %>
<% end %>
<% if condition[:omitted_job_class_count].positive? %>
- Additional job classes omitted: <%= condition[:omitted_job_class_count] %>
<% end %>
<% when "failed_attachment_scans" %>
Failed attachment scans: <%= condition[:total_count] %>
<% condition[:groups].each do |group| %>
- <%= group[:status_code] %>: <%= group[:count] %> failure(s); first <%= group[:first_failed_at] %>; most recent <%= group[:most_recent_failed_at] %>
<% end %>
<% when "stale_attachment_scans" %>
Stale pending attachment scans: <%= condition[:count] %>
- Oldest created at: <%= condition[:oldest_created_at] %>
- Most recent created at: <%= condition[:most_recent_created_at] %>
<% end %>

<% end %>
Investigate in an authenticated operational environment. Do not copy serialized job payloads, raw exception text, or attachment metadata into tickets or shared logs.
